WEBVTT

00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:13,460
I said to emails with photos of rashes and welts were you able to see though?

00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:21,340
Yes I was. Like I said before, it's very difficult to determine the cause of a

00:00:21,340 --> 00:00:25,580
rash sometimes. Well yeah, it's easy when you you know you go out and you rub

00:00:25,580 --> 00:00:30,420
against poison ivy and you get a rash. So that is a topical dermatitis where

00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:37,060
there is a rash because of a topical irritant. But when there is a systemic

00:00:37,060 --> 00:00:43,120
irritant that's causing a dermatitis of some kind, it's difficult to find out what

00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:50,260
that is because even if you took a sample of the pus of a rash or you took some

00:00:50,260 --> 00:00:54,060
sort of microscopic sample from the rash, you're still not going to see

00:00:54,060 --> 00:01:00,380
anything. Most I'm in the rash itself because the rash itself is a

00:01:00,380 --> 00:01:05,920
histamine inflammatory reaction due to some irritant. Well the irritant is

00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:15,280
necessarily present in the rash itself. So it's hard to analyze you know the

00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:20,560
cause of that rash sometimes. Anything that could cause inflammation that could

00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:26,440
cause a rash. Anything that could be an irritant could cause a rash. So you have

00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:34,120
to do some digging into what could be an irritant in that person's case. And

00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:39,880
that's not, but always an easy thing to figure out.

